cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the released models, please cite it as below."
title: "acophenotype: a Python suite for multi-representation acoustic phenotyping of speech"
abstract: >-
  Four Python packages released with the PhD thesis: voxmarkers (interpretable acoustic
  biomarkers), acophen-streams (SSL, vision and emotion representations), acophen-fusion
  (frozen fusion models trained on the Pitt Corpus) and acophenotype (end-to-end profile
  and HTML report). Pretrained models are distributed via the Hugging Face Hub.
  Research use only; not a medical device.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sviderski
    given-names: Marek
version: 0.1.1
license: MIT
keywords:
  - speech
  - acoustic biomarkers
  - dementia
  - Alzheimer's disease
  - multimodal fusion
repository-code: "https://github.com/tobiasSviderski/acophenotype"
